# Files excluded from test-coverage measurement (covr reads this automatically; one glob per line,
# relative to the package root). `.Rbuildignore`d, so it never ships in the tarball.
#
# The rule for this list: a file belongs here only when coverage is MEANINGLESS (the file is not
# hand-written R that a test could call) or IMPOSSIBLE (it needs a runtime we cannot start in a test
# process). "Untested but testable" does NOT belong here -- hiding that would remove the signal.

# --- Meaningless: auto-generated ------------------------------------------------------------
# Emitted by `jmvtools::prepare()` from the jamovi .a.yaml (CLAUDE.md: "auto-generated, do not
# edit"). 964 lines of option-class scaffolding that no R test can call, and that we must never
# hand-edit -- so a coverage figure for them is noise, and it dominated the headline number.
R/jmvtab.h.R
R/jmvtabreg.h.R

# --- Impossible: needs a live jamovi session ------------------------------------------------
# The R6 analysis backends. Their methods run inside jamovi's own Analysis lifecycle (jmvcore
# results objects, $state persistence, the option/results plumbing); there is no jamovi process in
# a testthat run. The engine-free logic they orchestrate is deliberately factored OUT into
# jmvtab-cache.R / jmvtabreg-cache.R / jmvtab-export.R, which ARE tested (87-93%).
R/jmvtab.b.R
R/jmvtabreg.b.R

# --- Deliberately NOT excluded --------------------------------------------------------------
# R/tab-steps-legacy.R    exported (superseded) public API -- tab_pct()/tab_tot()/tab_totaltab().
#                         Was 0% (its only test calls were commented out at test-tab.R:272-307);
#                         test-steps-legacy.R now covers it. Testable, so it stays measured.
# R/tab-parallel.R        real code, only under-measured because test-parallel-parity.R skips
#                         under covr (killed mirai daemons truncate covr's trace files). It is
#                         still run in full by devtools::test() and R-CMD-check on all 5 platforms.
